@database "duckduckgo_search"
@author "Enrico Ehrich"
@$VER: duckduckgo_search.guide 1.0 (30.09.2026)
@smartwrap

@node main "DuckDuckGo search"
@{h1}DuckDuckGo search

DuckDuckGo search gives an agent one tool that searches the web and
answers with a list of hits: title, address and a short snippet each. It
needs no account and no key. It finds pages; it does not read them -- an
agent that wants a page's text fetches it afterwards, for example with
the web scraper. Results are kept for a while, so asking the same thing
twice costs no second search. It has no hooks and no panel.

@{code}
For users
  @{"  Setting it up  " link setup}

For agents and developers
  @{"  The search tool  " link search}
  @{"  What the model sees  " link model}
@{body}
@endnode

@node search "The search tool"
@{h1}The search tool

The tool is named after the instance: @{tt}duckduckgo_search_web_search@{utt}
in the default setup. It sends the query through the @{tt}ddgs@{utt}
package and answers with the hits.

@{h2}Where the hits come from

Despite the name, not only from DuckDuckGo. @{tt}ddgs@{utt} asks several
search engines, a few at a time -- Wikipedia and Grokipedia first, then,
in a random order, Brave, DuckDuckGo, Google, Mojeek, Startpage and
Yahoo -- until it has enough hits, merges them (one entry per address, the longer
snippet wins) and ranks them against the query. Which engines answered
is not part of the answer; the address shows where a hit lives. The
search runs for the region "us-en" with moderate safe search; neither
can be changed.

@{h2}Parameters

The framework does not check the arguments against the schema; what
follows is what the code does with them.

@{table}
Parameter | Meaning
query | the search terms; required. Leading and trailing spaces are removed; empty answers an error
max_results | how many hits at most; default 10, also when null. A value below 1 is taken as 1, above 20 as 20, a fraction is cut (5.9 is 5), a number as text ("5") is read. Not a number: an error
ignore_cache | true: do not use a kept result, search again. A new result with hits replaces the kept one. Default false
cache_ttl | how long this result is kept, in seconds; default the server's @{tt}cache_ttl@{utt} (900). Not a number: the server's value. 0 or less: kept, but already expired
@{body}

@{h2}The answer

@{table}
Field | Meaning
engine | always "duckduckgo"
query | the query, without leading and trailing spaces
results | the hits, best first: @{tt}title@{utt}, @{tt}href@{utt} (the address) and @{tt}body@{utt} (the snippet)
error | only when the search failed or was refused, see below
cancelled | true when the agent's run was stopped before a search attempt
@{body}

@{code json}
{"engine": "duckduckgo", "query": "godot texture filter",
 "results": [
   {"title": "Texture filtering -- Godot Engine documentation",
    "href": "https://docs.godotengine.org/...",
    "body": "Godot supports several texture filtering modes ..."},
   ...]}
@{body}

Snippets are usually one to three sentences. A Wikipedia hit is the
exception: its snippet is the article's whole introduction, which can run
to a few thousand characters. There is at most one of those per search.

@{h2}Nothing found is not an error

A search where every engine answered and none had a hit comes back as
@{tt}results: []@{utt} without an @{tt}error@{utt}. An empty
@{tt}results@{utt} with an @{tt}error@{utt} means the search itself
failed. Only this difference tells "no hits for this query" from "the
search did not work".

@{h2}Retries and errors

A failed attempt -- rate limit, timeout, every engine failing -- is tried
again twice, after a pause of one to two and then two to three seconds. A
search that still fails answers @{tt}results: []@{utt} and the failure
in @{tt}error@{utt}; it never raises.

@{table}
error | When
Empty query | query is empty, missing or only spaces
max_results must be a whole number from 1 to 20, got 'many' | max_results is not a number
DuckDuckGo search failed for 'godot': RatelimitException: ... | all three attempts failed; the text names the last failure
Search cancelled by user | the agent's run was stopped before an attempt; also @{tt}cancelled: true@{utt}
@{body}

A stop is noticed only before an attempt, not while one is running. An
attempt waits up to about five seconds for each round of engines.

If @{tt}ddgs@{utt} is not installed the call does raise, with "Install
`ddgs` for the duckduckgo_search plugin: pip install ddgs": a missing
package must never look like a search that found nothing.

@{h2}What is kept

A result is kept per query and @{tt}max_results@{utt}; case and leading
or trailing spaces of the query do not matter, so "Godot " and "godot"
share one entry. A kept result is returned as it was stored, including
the query as first asked. An empty result is never kept: it is more
often a hiccup on the engines' side than a fact about the query, and the
next call asks again. The kept results are shared by every instance of
the plugin.

@{h2}An example

@{code json}
{"query": "godot texture filter"}
{"query": "python asyncio timeout", "max_results": 5}
{"query": "ddgs release notes", "ignore_cache": true}
@{body}
@endnode

@node model "What the model sees"
@{h1}What the model sees

@{h2}The tool

The description and the parameters come from the plugin's
@{tt}schema.yaml@{utt}, the same for every instance but the name:

@{code text}
Search the web with DuckDuckGo. Returns titles, URLs and snippets; no account needed. Snippets are short -- read a promising page with the scraper afterwards.
@{body}

query says "Search terms. Keywords work better than full sentences.",
ignore_cache "Bypass the cache and query DuckDuckGo again", cache_ttl
"Cache lifetime for this result in seconds (default from config)".
max_results has only its range 1 to 20 and its default 10, which the
code applies. The whole tool definition is about 800 characters.

@{h2}Errors, word for word

@{bullet}"Empty query"
@{bullet}"max_results must be a whole number from 1 to 20, got 'many'"
@{bullet}"DuckDuckGo search failed for 'godot': RatelimitException: ..."
@{bullet}"Search cancelled by user"
@{bullet}Without @{tt}ddgs@{utt}: "Tool 'duckduckgo_search_web_search'
execution failed: Install `ddgs` for the duckduckgo_search plugin: pip
install ddgs"

@{h2}The status line

"Searching: godot texture filter", then "10 results -- godot texture
filter" or "10 results (cached) -- ..." (the query cut to 60
characters). A failed search shows its error text, as does a refused
call.

@{h2}Tokens and cache

The tool definition is the same on every request, so the prompt cache
holds; the plugin adds nothing to the system prompt. The answer is an
ordinary tool result, appended. Measured: 10 hits about 4,300 to 4,600
characters, 20 hits about 9,700 -- the largest answer the tool can give,
apart from an unusually long Wikipedia introduction. Asking for fewer
hits is the way to keep it small.

@{h2}Known gaps

@{bullet}The hits come from several engines, not only DuckDuckGo; the
answer does not say which one found a hit.
@{bullet}Region and safe search are fixed (us-en, moderate).
@{bullet}A stop is noticed only between attempts.
@{bullet}Snippets are for choosing a page, not for answering from; read
the page before relying on it.
@endnode

@node setup "Setting it up"
@{h1}Setting it up

The plugin is on in the default configuration
(@{tt}config/plugins.yaml@{utt}), as the search for agents without a
Tavily key:

@{code yaml}
plugins:
  servers:
    duckduckgo_search:
      type: duckduckgo_search
      enabled: true
      cache_ttl: 900
@{body}

An agent sees the tool when its allowlist names it:

@{code yaml}
agent_config:
  tools:
    allowed:
      - "+duckduckgo_search/*"
@{body}

It needs internet access and the package @{tt}ddgs@{utt} (9.16 or
newer), which the plugin declares in its @{tt}plugin.toml@{utt}. Do not
install the older @{tt}duckduckgo-search@{utt} next to it: it is the same
project under its previous name, and against today's search pages it
returns no hits at all, without an error.

@{h2}Server settings

@{table}
Key | Default in code | Meaning
cache_ttl | 900 | seconds a result is kept, unless the call sets its own
cache_enabled | true | false: never keep or reuse a result
@{body}

The @{tt}config:@{utt} block of @{tt}schema.yaml@{utt} is not read; the
defaults above are the code's own.

@{h2}Where data lives

Kept results are files under @{tt}data/cache/duckduckgo_search/@{utt},
one per query. An expired entry is removed when it is next looked up;
@{tt}python -m agent_system.plugins.cache_manager clean --plugin
duckduckgo_search@{utt} removes all expired ones, @{tt}clear@{utt}
instead of @{tt}clean@{utt} all of them.

@{h2}A quick check

@{code text}
python -m plugins.duckduckgo_search --query "godot texture filter"
@{body}

runs one search from the command line (five hits by default,
@{tt}--max-results@{utt} changes it) and prints title, address and
snippet. It uses the same kept results as the agents.
@endnode
